# Public API base URL, inlined into the JS bundle at build/start time —
# not a secret, this is the same URL curl hits directly. Without this, the
# app falls back to guessing the backend lives on the dev machine's own LAN
# address (see src/api/config.ts's guessLanBaseUrl()), which only works when
# your phone is on the same WiFi as your laptop. Pointing this at Railway
# makes the app work from anywhere, matching how the backend is actually
# hosted. To test against a local `npm run dev` server instead, override in
# an untracked .env.local (already gitignored) rather than editing this file.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://ticker-production-95d9.up.railway.app
